
. * generated by run_all.py: the package root is the first argument
. args root

. global PKGROOT `"`root'"'

. cd `"`root'/02_code/10_analysis"'
<PACKAGE_ROOT>/02_code/10_analysis

. do "UP_C2_A1_09_natfirst.do" corrected2x 

. * UP_C2_A1_09_natfirst.do -- GENERATED by C2_A1_12_make_upair.py from C2_A1_0
> 9_natfirst.do; do not edit.
. * Changes: cluster variable pair_id -> unordered_pair_id (3 vce, 0 stack, 2 A
> 1_stack);
. * outputs in the sandbox folder ${OUTROOT}/${VINTAGE}_upair.
. /****************************************************************************
> ***
>  C2_A1_09_natfirst.do -- rerun C2, request R1-2.12 design (C): priority rever
> sal, final data only.
>  Usage (cwd = 02_code/10_analysis):  stata-mp -b -q do C2_A1_09_natfirst.do c
> orrected2x
>  Output: ${OUT}/results/A1_parts/A1_09.csv (A1_combine.py picks it up), ${OUT
> }/tables/A1_A1.5_m_natfirst.csv,
>          log, nflow records in ${OUT}/A1_nflow.csv.
>  Construction: per stored direction, nationality-first = nationality series w
> here it exists, residence as
>  fallback (the baseline is residence first, nationality fallback: COPY 01_bui
> ld_UN_Tourism.do:620-629), from
>  the snapshot master series (as C2_A1_08_overlap.do step 0; trips = thousand 
> trips x 1000, lines 667-669).
>  Quarantined residence cells (PAK; BLR->LIE visitors; PRY already missing in 
> the master) stay missing as
>  residence values under both rules: they are never used and never replaced. S
> ame direction from the opposite
>  row; bilateral = sum of the two directions; IHS as 01_prep.do.
>  Controls: the availability of a value is identical under both rules in every
>  direction (both use either
>  basis), hence has_both is identical (asserted row by row); the nationality-f
> irst model is fitted on the
>  baseline candidate rows and its e(sample) is compared with s_base_<m> (key-b
> y-key merge, zero mismatches
>  asserted, else identical observations by fixed point and the difference is r
> eported).
>  Comparison on identical observations: separate PPML fits and the stacked tes
> t (A1_stack: block-specific FE,
>  cluster by the original pair id, 1e-6 reproduction check; A1_00_programs.do)
> ; the same within the
>  same-basis subsample defined under both rules (both directions on one basis 
> under the baseline rule and
>  under the nationality-first rule).
>  Help consulted: ppmlhdfe.sthlp 2.3.4 (absorb(), vce(cluster), e(sample), e(N
> ), e(N_full), e(num_singletons),
>  e(num_separated), e(converged)); [R] test; [R] lincom; [D] merge; [D] isid; 
> [R] summarize (detail
>  percentiles); [P] postfile; nflow.sthlp 1.0.1. No data value is altered.
> *****************************************************************************
> **/
. args vintage

. clear all

. set more off

. set varabbrev off

. set linesize 200

. version 18.0

. do "00_config.do" `vintage'

. /*******************************************************************************
>  00_config.do  --  globals for one data vintage (analysis layer of the replication package)
> 
>  Usage (from another do-file, cwd = 02_code/10_analysis):  do 00_config.do <vintage>
>    <vintage> = corrected2x (revised baseline, default run)
>              | corrected | corrected2 (reconciliation switch, same data build)
>              | submitted (reconciliation switch, needs a second build with corrections off)
>  Every path is built from the package root ${PKGROOT}, which run_all.py passes as the first
>  argument of the generated wrapper do-file (_run.do pattern); nothing here is machine-specific.
>  Defines globals only and checks the Stata version.
> 
>  Vintages (see README.md, "Data-correction rules"):
>    corrected   = build with the correction rules on (code 490 -> TWN, Paraguay residence quarantine, flags)
>    corrected2  = corrected + quarantine of PAK residence 2020-2021 and BLR visitors-by-residence
>                  partner LIE 2020-2022 (same rule as Paraguay); 31-code outcome
>    corrected2x = corrected2 with the 30-code outcome (31-code basket minus HS 490700) = revised baseline
>    submitted   = original data as submitted (build with corrections off), for the reconciliation only
> *******************************************************************************/
. 
. args vintage

. if !inlist("`vintage'", "submitted", "corrected", "corrected2", "corrected2x") {
.     display as error "VINTAGE must be submitted, corrected, corrected2 or corrected2x; got [`vintage']"
.     exit 198
. }

